SCOPE OF THE MIT LICENCE IN THIS REPOSITORY

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the material in this repository that is mine
to license: the loop harness, its tests and scripts, the design notes, and the
output the loop itself generated in each dry run.

Two categories are not mine to license, and are excluded from that grant.

1. The question briefs — dry-runs/*/QUESTION.md

   These are LegalQuants' own assessment material, reproduced here because
   they are published in their public baselines repository at
   https://github.com/LegalQuants/lq-assess-machine-baselines. They are
   included for reference, so each run's output can be read against the brief
   it was answering. Nothing in LICENSE grants any right in them, and any
   reuse is a matter for LegalQuants rather than for me.

2. The source documents — dry-runs/OQ-010/documents/ and
   dry-runs/OQ-010-v2/documents/

   These are third-party public-domain records:

   - an 1827 handwritten probate bond from the Supreme Court of New South
     Wales (In the Goods of James Squire), via Wikimedia Commons;
   - a 1755 Virginia land indenture, digitised by the Augusta County Circuit
     Court Archive;
   - a page of a United States federal court filing (United States v.
     Manafort, D.D.C. 17-cr-201, Doc. 525);
   - a United States federal FOIA production.

   They were already in the public domain when obtained. They are not mine, I
   claim no copyright in them, and LICENSE neither adds to nor subtracts from
   their existing status. Provenance and attribution for each are recorded in
   the README of the run that uses it.
